  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 20.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ eac ah hlaforda gehwylc þæs formycle þearfe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he his men rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-a">And eac ah hlaforda gehwylc þæs formicele þearfe, þæt he his menn rihtlice heolde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ eac ah laforda gehwylc ðæs formyccle ðearfe, þæt he his men rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et unicuique domino magnum opus est, ut hominem suum recte deducat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ eac ah laforda gehwylc ðæs formyccle ðearfe þæt he his men rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And likewise it is the great duty of every lord to treat his men justly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und auch jeder der Herren hat dazu gar starke Verpflichtung, dass er seine Untergebenen rechtlich halte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And also every lord has very great need to treat his men rightly.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G</note>
      </div>
    </body>
